                <pb facs="0181" n="75" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg75"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Baron Moncheur to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Belgium</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-05-05"><hi rendition="#italic">May 5,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>: In continuation of the
                    communication I had the honor to address to your excellency on March 26 last,
                    respecting the proposed convention relative to collisions and assistance at sea,
                    I am instructed to inform you that Brazil, the Dominican Republic, and Roumania
                    have notified their adhesion to the draft.</p>
                <p>I gladly embrace this opportunity, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bn. Moncheur.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
